 * @endif
 * 
 * @if RST_SUPPORT
 * @embedRstVerbatim{
 * .. admonition:: Note
 * 
 *    Recipe build was tested in radioconda environment for Windows and Linux platforms.}
 * @else
 * @note Recipe build was tested in radioconda environment for Windows and Linux platforms.
 * @endif 
 * 
 * @section gnuradio-limesuiteng_recipe_struct Recipe structure
 * 
 * A full conda recipe is made out of three main files:
 * 
 * - meta.yaml
 * - bld.bat (For Windows platform)
 * - bld.sh (For Linux/MacOS platforms)
 * 
 * Meta.yaml file is used to specify required dependencies for build. When building gnuradio-limesuiteng plugin from recipe, it is important to keep track of the following dependency versions:
 * 
 * - python
 * - numpy
 * - pybind11
 * - volk
 * - boost
 * 
 * Required exact versions of dependencies can be found out by inspecting the recipe meta.yaml file of gnuradio package. Failure to match the correct dependency versions can result in plugin 
 * operation failure. Scripts bld.bat and bld.sh are used for the actual build. Inside the scripts you can add additional CMake flags and any other commands that will be executed in command 
 * line/terminal environment.
 * 
 * More details about <a href="https://docs.conda.io/projects/conda-build/en/stable/resources/index.html">conda recipes</a>.
 * 
 * @section gnuradio-limesuiteng_recipe_build Recipe build steps
 * 
 * To build the plugin, Lime Suite NG conda package must be built and installed inside the current conda environment. To start the build process, execute the following commands:
 * 
 * @code{.bash}
 *    conda activate <custom env name>
 *    cd <repo root>\plugins\gr-limesuiteng
 *    conda-build .conda\recipe\ -m .conda\build_config.yaml
 * @endcode
 * 
 * Conda will start building the package. The ``build_config.yaml`` file alongside the ``-m`` flag enables package build from locally stored source code. To build from the git ``develop`` branch, omit the flag and arguments.
 *
 * After a successful build, the conda package is populated in the ``<radioconda install dir>\envs\<your custom env>\conda-bld\`` directory with the following name structure: ``gnuradio-limesuiteng-version-build_string.conda``.
 * 
 * @if RST_SUPPORT
 * @embedRstVerbatim{
 * .. admonition:: Warning
 * 
 *    Currently gnuradio-limesuiteng plugin package cannot be built for ``gnuradio=3.10.12.0``, because it requires ``boost=1.86`` package which is currently not available in conda environment. 
 *    In order to pass the plugin build, user must specify gnuradio version in meta.yaml file as stated below in important note.}
 * @else
 * @warning Currently gnuradio-limesuiteng plugin package cannot be built for ``gnuradio=3.10.12.0``, because it requires ``boost=1.86`` package which is currently not available in conda environment. 
 * In order to pass the plugin build, user must specify gnuradio version in meta.yaml file as stated below in important note.
 * @endif
 * 
 * @if RST_SUPPORT
 * @embedRstVerbatim{
 * .. admonition:: Important
 * 
 *    To target a specific gnuradio version plugin build, edit the meta.yaml file inside ``recipe`` directory. Specify required version for all entries of gnuradio package. 
 *    Example: ``gnuradio =3.10.10.0``. If gnuradio package version is not specified, plugin will be built for the newest gnuradio version.}
 * @else
 * @important To target a specific gnuradio version plugin build, edit the meta.yaml file inside ``recipe`` directory. Specify required version for all entries of gnuradio package. 
 * Example: ``gnuradio =3.10.10.0``. If gnuradio package version is not specified, plugin will be built for the newest gnuradio version.
 * @endif
 *    
 * @section gnuradio-limesuiteng_pckg_install Installing built package
 * 
 * To test the built gnuradio-limesuiteng plugin, the package must be installed using the ``conda install`` command. Before installing the package, the path to the local channel for the conda tool must be specified.
 * To install the locally built gnuradio-limesuiteng package, execute the following command:
 * 
 * @code{.bash}
 *    conda install gnuradio-limesuiteng
 * @endcode
 * 
 * Optionally, you can specify version ``gnuradio-limesuiteng=1.0.0`` or version and build string ``limesuiteng=1.0.0=py312hfd7c3e5_0`` if there are multiple versions of the same package.
 * 
 */